@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### Forgot password (always returns the same message). Copy the token from the server log.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"test@example.com"}

### Reset with the token from the log link (?token=...)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{"token":"PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_LOG","newPassword":"newpassword123"}

### Change password (logged in)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"currentPassword":"password123","newPassword":"anotherpass456"}

### View profile
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update profile
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"firstName":"Test","lastName":"User","phone":"+27 82 123 4567","monthlyIncome":15000.00}

### Upload a profile picture (IntelliJ: set a real file path)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/me/picture
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="me.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./me.png
--WebAppBoundary--

### Fetch it back
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me/picture
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ADMIN: list users / deactivate one
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/2/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"enabled":false}
